n  files  (the\n   \"Software\"),  to  deal in  the  Software  without restriction,  including\n   without  limitation the  rights  to use,  copy,  modify, merge,  publish,\n   distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit\n   persons  to whom  the Software  is  furnished to  do so,  subject to  the\n   following conditions:\n\n   The above copyright  notice and this permission notice  shall be included\n   in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n   THE  SOFTWARE  IS  PROVIDED  \"AS  IS\",  WITHOUT  WARRANTY  OF  ANY  KIND,\n   EXPRESS  OR IMPLIED,  INCLUDING  BUT  NOT LIMITED  TO  THE WARRANTIES  OF\n   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN\n   NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR  COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,\n   DAMAGES OR  OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER  IN AN  ACTION OF CONTRACT,  TORT OR\n   OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE\n   USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n\n   SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n*/"] [85 1 "/* Hash table related internal API\n                            __  __            _\n                         ___\\ \\/ /_ __   __ _| |_\n                        / _ \\\\  /| '_ \\ / _` | __|\n                       |  __//  \\| |_) | (_| | |_\n                        \\___/_/\\_\\ .__/ \\__,_|\\__|\n                                 |_| XML parser\n\n   Copyright (c) 2026 Sebastian Pipping <sebastian@pipping.org>\n   Licensed under the MIT license:\n\n   Permission is  hereby granted,  free of charge,  to any  person obtaining\n   a  copy  of  this  software   and  associated  documentation  files  (the\n   \"Software\"),  to  deal in  the  Software  without restriction,  including\n   without  limitation the  rights  to use,  copy,  modify, merge,  publish,\n   distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit\n   persons  to whom  the Software  is  furnished to  do so,  subject to  the\n   following conditions:\n\n   The above copyright  notice and this permission notice  shall be included\n   in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n   THE  SOFTWARE  IS  PROVIDED  \"AS  IS\",  WITHOUT  WARRANTY  OF  ANY  KIND,\n   EXPRESS  OR IMPLIED,  INCLUDING  BUT  NOT LIMITED  TO  THE WARRANTIES  OF\n   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN\n   NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR  COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,\n   DAMAGES OR  OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER  IN AN  ACTION OF CONTRACT,  TORT OR\n   OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE\n   USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n\n   SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n   The port to Go (queue 202e): Copyright (c) the Arbace authors, under the same MIT license.\n*/"] [122 1 "// ---- xmlparse.c: from its top to the end of XML_ParserStruct and the"] [123 1 "// MALLOC/REALLOC/FREE macros (C lines 1-842), with hash_table.h. The"] [124 1 "// functions poolAppendChar and poolAppendChars (C lines 678-700, among the"] [125 1 "// declarations) are ported here too; xmlparse_api.go starts with"] [126 1 "// expat_heap_stat (C line 844). ----"] [128 1 "// The configuration (expat_config.h): XML_NS, XML_DTD, XML_GE 1,"] [129 1 "// XML_CONTEXT_BYTES 1024, BYTEORDER 1234, XML_POOR_ENTROPY."] [132 1 "// XML_UNICODE is not defined:"] [133 1 "//"] [134 1 "//\t#define XML_ENCODE_MAX XML_UTF8_ENCODE_MAX"] [135 1 "//\t#define XmlConvert XmlUtf8Convert"] [136 1 "//\t#define XmlGetInternalEncoding XmlGetUtf8InternalEncoding"] [137 1 "//\t#define XmlGetInternalEncodingNS XmlGetUtf8InternalEncodingNS"] [138 1 "//\t#define XmlEncode XmlUtf8Encode"] [139 1 "//\t#define MUST_CONVERT(enc, s) (! (enc)->isUtf8)"] [140 1 "//\ttypedef char ICHAR;"] [157 1 "// XML_T(x) and XML_L(x) are x."] [161 1 "/* Round up n to be a multiple of sz, where sz is a power of 2. */"] [164 1 "/* Do safe (NULL-aware) pointer arithmetic */"] [172 1 "// EXPAT_MIN, as xmlparse.c uses it (size_t operands)."] [180 1 "// ---- hash_table.h ----"] [184 1 "// NAMED is the common head of ELEMENT_TYPE, ATTRIBUTE_ID, PREFIX, ENTITY and"] [185 1 "// NAME_AND_DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE: each holds `name KEY` first and implements"] [186 1 "// namedKey. A cast `(ELEMENT_TYPE *)lookup(...)` is"] [187 1 "// `x, _ := lookup(...).(*ELEMENT_TYPE)` (nil when lookup returns NULL)."] [199 2 "// Go's own: this table is an ELEMENT_TYPE's defaultAttForName, so that"] [200 2 "// lookup's createSize sizeof_NAME_AND_DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE (24) is told"] [201 2 "// apart from sizeof_ATTRIBUTE_ID (24 too). Set by newNamed when it"] [202 2 "// makes an ELEMENT_TYPE; hashTableInit leaves it alone."] [206 1 "// HASH_TABLE_ITER: p and end, C's NAMED ** into table->v, are indexes into v."] [213 1 "// newNamed is the Go side of lookup's `table->v[i] = MALLOC(table->parser,"] [214 1 "// createSize); memset(table->v[i], 0, createSize);`: the zero value of the"] [215 1 "// type createSize names (after MALLOC accounted createSize). The caller then"] [216 1 "// sets `*table.v[i].namedKey() = name`."] [236 1 "// sizeofNamed is the size C's lookup gave the object (for FREE)."] [253 1 "// ---- xmlparse.c's types ----"] [255 1 "/*\nFor probing (after a collision) we need a step size relative prime\n\n\tto the hash table size, which is a power of 2. We use double-hashing,\n\tsince we can calculate a second hash value cheaply by taking those bits\n\tof the first hash value that were discarded (masked out) when the table\n\tindex was calculated: index = hash & mask, where mask = table->size - 1.\n\tWe limit the maximum step size to table->size / 4 (mask >> 2) and make\n\tit odd, since odd numbers are always relative prime to a power of 2.\n*/"] [274 26 "/* must be a multiple of sizeof(XML_Char) */"] [310 1 "/*\nTAG represents an open element.\n\n\tThe name of the element is stored in both the document and API\n\tencodings.  The memory buffer 'buf' is a separately-allocated\n\tmemory area which stores the name.  During the XML_Parse()/\n\tXML_ParseBuffer() when the element is open, the memory for the 'raw'\n\tversion of the name (in the document encoding) is shared with the\n\tdocument buffer.  If the element is open across calls to\n\tXML_Parse()/XML_ParseBuffer(), the buffer is re-allocated to\n\tcontain the 'raw' name as well.\n\n\tA parser reuses these structures, maintaining a list of allocated\n\tTAG objects in a free list.\n*/"] [326 21 "/* parent of this element */"] [327 21 "/* tagName in the original encoding */"] [329 25 "/* tagName in the API encoding */"] [330 2 "// union { char *raw; XML_Char *str; } buf: XML_Char is char, so both"] [331 2 "// members are this one Ptr: tag->buf.raw and tag->buf.str are tag.buf."] [332 15 "/* buffer for name components */"] [333 15 "/* end of the buffer */"] [340 18 "/* length in XML_Chars */"] [341 18 "/* # of processed bytes - when suspended */"] [347 17 "/* true if entity has not been completely processed */"] [348 2 "/* An entity can be open while being already completely processed (!hasMore).\n\t   The reason is the delayed closing of entities until their inner\n\t   entities are processed and closed */"] [352 19 "/* true if declared in internal subset outside PE */"] [369 1 "// BLOCK is struct block: s, C's flexible array member XML_Char s[], is the"] [370 1 "// block's characters (len(s) == size); a pool's start, ptr and end are"] [371 1 "// Ptr{B: block.s, ...}. The block's C size is offsetof_BLOCK_s + size."] [387 1 "/*\nThe XML_Char before the name is used to determine whether\n\n\tan attribute has been specified.\n*/"] [407 1 "// This structure allows mapping attribute names to instances of"] [408 1 "// `DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE`."] [410 2 "// Member `name` goes first to make this structure compatible with structure"] [411 2 "// `NAMED` (further up), which is needed to support use of structure"] [412 2 "// `NAME_AND_DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE` in a hash table as implemented by function"] [413 2 "// `lookup` (further down)."] [415 2 "// We would store a `DEFAULT_ATTRIBUTE *` here but the backing array"] [416 2 "// can be reallocated which would invalidate the pointer. Using an index"] [417 2 "// into the array instead, avoids that problem."] [419 2 "// This is set to `false` by function `lookup`."] [431 1 "// ELEMENT_TYPE: defaultAtts (C's malloc'd array, allocDefaultAtts entries)"] [432 1 "// is a slice of allocDefaultAtts entries."] [445 1 "// DTD: scaffold (scaffSize entries) and scaffIndex (scaffIndexSize"] [446 1 "// entries) are slices."] [454 2 "/* false once a parameter entity reference has been skipped */"] [456 2 "/* true once an internal or external PE reference has been encountered;\n\t   this includes the reference to an external subset */"] [460 2 "/* indicates if external PE has been read */"] [464 2 "/* === scaffolding for building content model === */"] [489 27 "/* WFC: PE Between Declarations */"] [496 50 "/* bytes directly passed to the Expat parser */"] [497 50 "/* intermediate bytes produced during entity\n\t   expansion */"] [499 19 "/* i.e. do not account, was accounted already */"] [508 37 "// >=1.0"] [514 36 "// updated live only for debug level >=2"] [516 37 "// >=1.0"] [527 1 "// Processor: C's `typedef enum XML_Error Processor(...)`; m_processor"] [528 1 "// (Processor *) is a Processor."] [531 1 "// The static Processor declarations (prologProcessor, ...,"] [532 1 "// internalEntityProcessor) and the other forward declarations are the"] [533 1 "// functions of the parts; their Go signatures are in stubs_api.go,"] [534 1 "// stubs_doc.go and stubs_dtd.go until the parts replace them."] [559 2 "// Detect and prevent integer overflow"] [574 59 "// write ONLY in runtests.c"] [576 1 "// XML_ParserStruct is struct XML_ParserStruct, every field in C's order"] [577 1 "// (XML_DTD's and XML_GE's included), and m_appAtts, Go's own (see"] [578 1 "// appAttsView)."] [580 2 "/* The first member must be m_userData so that the XML_GetUserData\n\t   macro works. */"] [585 2 "// How the four parse buffer pointers below relate in time and space:"] [586 2 "//"] [587 2 "//   m_buffer <= m_bufferPtr <= m_bufferEnd  <= m_bufferLim"] [588 2 "//   |           |              |               |"] [589 2 "//   <--parsed-->|              |               |"] [590 2 "//               <---parsing--->|               |"] [591 2 "//                              <--unoccupied-->|"] [592 2 "//   <---------total-malloced/realloced-------->|"] [594 18 "// malloc/realloc base pointer of parse buffer"] [596 18 "// first character to be parsed"] [597 18 "// past last character to be parsed"] [598 18 "// allocated end of m_buffer"] [602 40 "/* used in heuristic to avoid O(n^2) */"] [636 51 "// void *: XmlInitUnknownEncoding's mem"] [639 2 "// Application callback invoked by callUnknownEncodingConvert."] [674 46 "// m_attsSize entries"] [675 46 "// nsAttsSize (1 << m_nsAttsPower) entries"] [697 2 "// Go's own: the array `(const XML_Char **)parser->m_atts`, which C lays"] [698 2 "// over m_atts' memory (storeAtts' appAtts, the atts doContent hands the"] [699 2 "// start element handler). Not accounted: it is m_atts' memory in C."] [703 1 "// appAttsView is `(const XML_Char **)parser->m_atts`: as many pointers as"] [704 1 "// m_atts' memory holds in C (m_attsSize * sizeof(ATTRIBUTE) /"] [705 1 "// sizeof(XML_Char *)), kept in m_appAtts. C writes appAtts[k] only after it"] [706 1 "// has read m_atts[k*8/32] ... (storeAtts reads each ATTRIBUTE before the"] [707 1 "// pointers reach it), so a separate array behaves as the overlay."] [718 1 "// ---- MALLOC, REALLOC, FREE (XML_GE == 1: the allocation tracker) ----"] [719 1 "//"] [720 1 "// The Go object is allocated by the caller; these account C's sizes and"] [721 1 "// refuse as C's do (false is C's NULL):"] [722 1 "//"] [723 1 "//\tMALLOC(parser, size) bool             then x := new(T) / make([]T, n) / Ptr{B: make([]byte, size)}"] [724 1 "//\tREALLOC(parser, oldSize, size) bool   then grow the slice into a new one (copy)"] [725 1 "//\tFREE(parser, size)                    the size the block was given"] [726 1 "//"] [727 1 "// A NULL block is the size NULL_BLOCK (blockSize, ptrBlock make it): FREE of"] [728 1 "// NULL_BLOCK does nothing (expat_free's `if (ptr == NULL) return;`), REALLOC"] [729 1 "// of NULL_BLOCK is MALLOC (expat_realloc's first test), and REALLOC to size 0"] [730 1 "// frees and returns false. C's __LINE__ of the macros is lost (0): it shows"] [731 1 "// only in EXPAT_MALLOC_DEBUG's report."] [732 1 "//"] [733 1 "// The bodies are xmlparse_api.go's (stubs_api.go until then)."] [735 1 "// NULL_BLOCK is the size of a NULL pointer: no C block can have it, since"] [736 1 "// expat_malloc refuses SIZE_MAX - size < sizeof(size_t) + EXPAT_MALLOC_PADDING."] [739 1 "// blockSize is size, or NULL_BLOCK when the pointer is NULL."] [747 1 "// ptrBlock is the size of a MALLOC'd character block (len(p.B)), or NULL_BLOCK."]] :go/pos {:name [120 9] :package [120 1]} :go/semis []} (go/file "xmlparse_types.go" :imports [])

;; ---- xmlparse.c: from its top to the end of XML_ParserStruct and the
;; MALLOC/REALLOC/FREE macros (C lines 1-842), with hash_table.h. The
;; functions poolAppendChar and poolAppendChars (C lines 678-700, among the
;; declarations) are ported here too; xmlparse_api.go starts with
;; expat_heap_stat (C line 844). ----



